ll>Claude 3.5 S</cell><cell>80 (26.67%) 17*</cell><cell>67 (26.91%) 17</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>GPT-4o</cell><cell>74 (24.67%) 21</cell><cell>62 (24.90%) 21</cell></row><row><cell>OpenDevin+CodeAct v1.8 [17]</cell><cell>Claude 3.5 S</cell><cell>80 (26.67%) 17*</cell><cell>65 (26.10%) 20</cell></row><row><cell>Aider [37]</cell><cell>GPT-4o+ Claude 3.5 S</cell><cell>79 (26.33%) 20</cell><cell>66 (26.51%) 18*</cell></row><row><cell>SWE-agent [101]</cell><cell>Claude 3.5 S</cell><cell>69 (23.00%) 23</cell><cell>58 (23.29%) 22</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>GPT-4o</cell><cell>55 (18.33%) 28</cell><cell>45 (18.07%) 27*</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>GPT-4</cell><cell>54 (18.00%) 29</cell><cell>42 (16.87%) 29</cell></row><row><cell>AppMap Navie [5]</cell><cell>GPT-4o</cell><cell>65 (21.67%) 24</cell><cell>56 (22.49%) 23*</cell></row><row><cell>AutoCodeRover [108]</cell><cell>GPT-4</cell><cell>57 (19.00%) 27</cell><cell>45 (18.07%) 27*</cell></row><row><cell>RAG [101]</cell><cell>Claude 3 Opus</cell><cell>13 (4.33%) 30</cell><cell>10 (4.02%) 30</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>GPT-4</cell><cell>8 (2.67%) 32</cell><cell>5 (2.01%) 32</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>Claude-2</cell><cell>9 (3.00%) 31</cell><cell>6 (2.41%) 31</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>GPT-3.5</cell><cell>1 (0.33%) 33</cell><cell>0 (0.00%) 33</cell></row><row><cell>AGENTLESS</cell><cell>GPT-4o</cell><cell>96 (32.00%) 9</cell><cell>84 (33.73%) 9</cell></row></table></figure>\n<figure xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" type=\"table\" xml:id=\"tab_5\"><head>Table 6 :</head><label>6</label><figDesc>Performance on SWE-bench Verified.</figDesc><table><row><cell>Tool</cell><cell>LLM</cell><cell>% Resolved</cell></row><row><cell>Tools [11]</cell><cell cols=\"2\">Claude 3.5 Sonnet (20241022) 245 (49.00%)</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>Claude 3.5 Haiku</cell><cell>203 (40.60%)</cell></row><row><cell>Solver [21]</cell><cell>NA</cell><cell>227 (45.40%)</cell></row><row><cell>Gru [20]</cell><cell>NA</cell><cell>226 (45.20%)</cell></row><row><cell>Honeycomb [10]</cell><cell>NA</cell><cell>203 (40.60%)</cell></row><row><cell>Amazon Q Developer-v2 [4]</cell><cell>NA</cell><cell>194 (38.80%)</cell></row><row><cell>Factory Code Droid [9]</cell><cell>NA</cell><cell>185 (37.00%)</cell></row><row><cell>Amazon Q Developer [4]</cell><cell>NA</cell><cell>128 (25.60%)</cell></row><row><cell>Composio SWEkit [8]</cell><cell>Claude 3.5 Sonnet</cell><cell>203 (40.60%)</cell></row><row><cell>AutoCodeRover-v2 [6]</cell><cell>GPT-4o</cell><cell>192 (38.40%)</cell></row><row><cell>SWE-agent [101]</cell><cell>Claude 3.5 Sonnet</cell><cell>168 (33.60%)</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>GPT-4o</cell><cell>116 (23.20%)</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>GPT-4</cell><cell>112 (22.40%)</cell></row><row><cell>Alibaba Lingma Agent [13]</cell><cell>Lingma SWE-GPT 72b</cell><cell>144 (28.80%)</cell></row><row><cell>AppMap Navie [5]</cell><cell>GPT-4o</cell><cell>131 (26.20%)</cell></row><row><cell>AGENTLESS</cell><cell>GPT-4o</cell><cell>194 (38.80%)</cell></row></table></figure>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"1\" xml:id=\"foot_0\"><p>If we directly use the PASS TO PASS tests the performance on SWE-bench Lite will be 98.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"2\" xml:id=\"foot_1\"><p>Note that the ground truth patch is only applied here to evaluate the test quality, and is not used during the AGENTLESS process for selecting the reproduction tests.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"3\" xml:id=\"foot_2\"><p>These types of problems still exist in the benchmark despite claims that they have been completely removed by the filtering process according to SWE-bench Lite.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"4\" xml:id=\"foot_3\"><p>Sadly the bike is currently broken.</p></note>\n\t\t</body>\n\t\t<back>\n\n\t\t\t<div type=\"acknowledgement\">\n<div><head>Acknowledgments</head><p>We thank <rs type=\"person\">Jiawei Liu</rs> and <rs type=\"person\">Yuxiang Wei</rs> for providing some of the resources used to run the experiments. One of the authors would like to thank <rs type=\"person\">Jun Yang</rs> for generously gifting his old bike <ref type=\"bibr\" target=\"#b2\">4</ref> which allowed the author to travel faster and thus increasing research speed.</p></div>\n\t\t\t</div>\t\t\t<div type=\"references\">\n\n\t\t\t\t<listBibl>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b0\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<ptr target=\"https://github.com/swe-bench/experiments/blob/main/evaluation/lite/20240612_IBM_Research_Agent101/README.md/\" />\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">101: A Software Engineering Agent for Code Assistance developed by IBM Research</title>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2024\">2024</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b1\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title/>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Sima</forename><surname>Alex</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<ptr target=\"https://github.com/swe-bench/experiments/tree/main/evaluation/lite/20240706_sima_gpt4o\" />\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2024\">2024</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b2\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Amazon Q Developer The most capable generative AI-powered assistant for software development</title>\n\t\t<ptr target=\"https://aws.amazon.com/q/developer//\" />\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2024\">2024</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b3\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<ptr target=\"https://appmap.io/blog/2024/06/20/appmap-navie-swe-bench-leader/\" />\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">AppMap speedruns to the top of the SWE Bench Leaderboard</title